---
description: Browser/TypeScript boundary rules for the emulator UI and worker
globs: web/**/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Web boundary

- Emulator execution runs in a Worker; UI thread owns canvas, input, and storage UX only.
- Talk to Wasm through a narrow typed API; do not reach into Rust internals from ad-hoc JS.
- v86 compatibility lives in `web/src/v86-compat/` as an adapter — do not reshape the core API to match v86 quirks.
- Persist disks via IndexedDB/OPFS behind a storage interface; keep paths swappable.
- Never put instruction semantics or device models in TypeScript.

# Checks

- Prefer Playwright for smoke boot/UI flows once the harness exists.
- Keep worker message types versioned when changing the protocol.
